      "tempo": 92,
      "tonicOctave": 4,
      "notes": "Four notes, and the pentatonic fence comes down: every call touches degree 6 or degree -1, the scale step that sits a semitone off the tonic. Major key on purpose - the natural minor the instrument writes has no such step, and 4.1 spends no chromatics. Ruling 2026-08-11: every degrees rung this early starts ON the tonic - sussing an unanchored first note is a later skill. Candidate d leads for that reason; a and c start off-tonic and wait.",
